  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "The snake copies the feints",
  "description": "An area of about 20 × 20 metres. Split the players into groups of four or five, each player with a ball. Each group is a snake: the players dribble in a line one behind the other, a few metres apart, and follow the first player wherever they go.\n\nThe first player decides: they turn, change speed and now and then do a feint and dribble, for example a step-over and then away the other way. Everyone behind does the same feint in the same place. After about a minute the coach calls \"change!\" – the first player curves out and joins the back of the line, and the next player takes over.\n\nVariants: the coach calls which feint to use, or lets each new head of the snake show one of their own. Several snakes in the same area make everyone look up. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Look up between touches so you see what the player in front does."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Sell the feint – a big body movement, then away quickly."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Keep your gap to the player in front, not too close and not too far."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "At the front: show it clearly, and mix left and right."
    }
  ],
